            x[n,t] ~ normal( theta[n,t], Sigma );
        }

Just my two cents (not much experience with stan, but after having played IRTs with JAGS for a while) :

The "sort" version might have label switching problems that the "differences" version may avoid. But specifying the variance is a bit more complex.

This might be sampler -implementation dependent.

HTH

