On Jul 15, 2014, at 2:44 AM, Soga Shota <soga....@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hi Bob,
>
>    The binomial-binomial model will be used in industrial application. Actually, my model is more complicated: binomial-binomial-logitnormal model.
>
>    log_sum_exp is a very interesting function. so log_sum_exp(vec) basically does log(sum(exp(vec))).
> It is quite useful in simplifying marginalization.

The important feature of log_sum_exp is that it won't overflow with
the exp() operation in either values or derivatives.  It also has
analytic derivatives so it's faster than calling log(sum(exp(vec)))
and takes less memory.

- Bob

